&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wolt Market/HOP is Wolt/Deliveroo’s owned and operated grocery business, focused on delivering the best customer experience through high-quality selection, strong availability, and fast delivery. As 1P continues to scale across multiple countries, we are looking for a Manager, Strategy &amp;amp; Operations to help drive sustainable topline growth and bottomline performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role works closely with the Head of Wolt Mart / HOP&amp;nbsp; and Regional General Managers (RGMs) to define strategic priorities, drive key growth initiatives, and ensure delivery of financial and operational targets. The person will act as a key partner to Marketing, Finance, Category Management, and other global functional teams, ensuring alignment between strategy, planning, and execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines strategic thinking with strong execution ownership, requiring exceptional analytical skills, structured problem solving, and the ability to lead cross-functional initiatives across 30+ markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Business Performance Ownership (Topline &amp;amp; Bottomline)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Head of Wolt Market / HOP and RGMs to drive sustainable growth and profitability across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and manage topline (GOV, orders, basket size) and bottomline (contribution margin, EBITDA, cost efficiency) performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify performance gaps, diagnose root causes, and drive corrective actions across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build forecasting models and performance tracking frameworks to ensure visibility and accountability against targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Strategic Planning &amp;amp; Financial Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance on annual planning, forecasting, and target setting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of long-term growth plans, investment cases, and strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment between financial targets and operational execution across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor performance vs plan and drive actions to close gaps where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Growth Initiatives &amp;amp; Marketing Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing to define and execute growth initiatives across acquisition, retention, and basket size expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize high-impact growth levers and ensure effective execution across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and evaluate impact of growth initiatives and continuously optimize based on performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of scalable playbooks to drive consistent growth across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Cross Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Category Management, Product, Operations, and other global teams to drive key strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional projects end-to-end, from problem definition to execution and impact measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable tools, processes, and operating models that enable strong execution across 30+ countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong alignment between global strategy and local market execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Data, Analytics &amp;amp; Performance Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Looker, Excel, and other BI tools to analyze business performance and identify actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards, models, and performance tracking tools to support decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex data into clear insights and strategic recommendations for senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support experimentation and test-and-learn approaches to optimize performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant experience in Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, management consulting, investment banking, tech companies, or high-growth retail/e-commerce environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced, high-growth, and cross-functional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with financial planning, growth strategy, or operational performance management is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Excel, including financial modelling, forecasting, and scenario analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience using BI tools such as Looker to extract insights and drive decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data-driven mindset with ability to translate data into actionable business recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL experience is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Strategic Thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding structured problem-solving skills with ability to break down complex and ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify high-impact opportunities and prioritize effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business judgment and ability to connect strategy with operational execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work closely with senior stakeholders, including General Managers and global functional leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills across global and local teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence without authority and drive alignment across multiple functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with demonstrated experience leading cross-functional initiatives end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and workstreams simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership mindset with strong bias toward action and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full professional proficiency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a global, fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, proactive, and highly motivated individual with strong ownership mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/GoL541_xj9w&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;About Wolt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Product Manager to own our search experience that millions of customers land on when they open DoorDash, Wolt, or Deliveroo, and the single biggest lever we have on what they find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits in our Core Consumer organisation in the Search domain, which is responsible for the in-app experience. You&#39;ll be building on a global stack, and your roadmap will be a mix: global platform problems that apply worldwide, global capabilities we&#39;re accelerating into EMEA markets, and EMEA-specific problems worth solving properly rather than working around.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Search is where customers tell us exactly what they want. Getting it right across restaurants, grocery, and retail - in every language we operate in - is one of the highest-intent and hardest problems in the app.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query understanding, Autosuggestions and AI/ML problems in the Search domain&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where conversational and agentic search changes how customers get to a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Making search work across three brands, multiple languages, and query behaviour that differs market by market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our humble expectations&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a product leader more than a feature owner. Someone who can find the problems that matter most, for customers and for the business, and make the case for solving them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring proven experience as a Product Manager in Consumer, or on another relevance- or ranking-driven consumer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate fluency with search measurement and know how to actually move it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You show strong product judgment, backed by data literacy and customer insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work backwards from the customer problem, and you can weigh that against the most urgent business problems at the same time, rather than treating it as a side you have to pick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically: you can zoom out to where the domain should be in two years, then zoom back in on what we should ship next quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity and genuinely flexible. This industry is changing fast, AI most of all, and the plan we write in January won&#39;t be the plan in June.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work deeply with ML and engineering on relevance and ranking, without needing to be an ML expert yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about what AI actually changes for customers, and you can tell real value from hype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build a case and bring people with you: engineering, design, analytics, and local market teams across three brands and many markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You do your best work with range: global platform thinking one week, a specific market&#39;s reality the next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Next steps&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position will be filled as soon as we find the right person, so make sure to apply as soon as you realize you really, really want to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ncz4s_oBczc?si=FzuwoSOLcv5WZVRN&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs, the company behind the open observability cloud, is founded on the principles of open source, open standards, open ecosystems, and open culture. Grafana Cloud, our fully managed observability platform, is flexible and built for scale. With Grafana Cloud&#39;s actually useful AI, organizations can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data to move at the speed of their ambitions. Today, more than 35 million users and 7,000+ customers – including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce – trust Grafana Labs to ensure reliability of their applications and systems, resolve incidents quickly, and optimize their telemetry to reduce noise and cost. We are a 100% remote company with 1,600+ team members across 40+ countries, and we’re backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a fully remote position and we&#39;re considering candidates in Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Product Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Product Manager at Grafana Labs, you&#39;ll develop a vision and strategy for your product domain. You will own your product’s roadmap, collateral, and market research, and you will collaborate with Grafana leadership on fine-tuning your product’s goals. You will be the primary advocate and expert in your area, with a strong ability to communicate needs, functionality, and details effectively both to external customers and internal stakeholders. The teams and people you will be interacting with will be 100% remote and globally distributed, so strong and proactive communication is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Managers are the bridge that connect Engineering, Design, and UX to GTM. You are a facilitator who ensures the free flow of information across these teams and are expected to be technically proficient when representing our products to our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Staff Product Manager for OpenTelemetry Experience, you’ll own the end-to-end journey for helping people and agents instrument workloads and successfully send useful OpenTelemetry data to Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to make Grafana Cloud the easiest and most trusted destination for OpenTelemetry workloads. You’ll reduce the uncertainty, complexity, and failure points users encounter between deciding to adopt OpenTelemetry and receiving healthy, correctly attributed, and actionable telemetry in Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teams can instrument workloads, directly or with the help of coding agents, through OpenTelemetry SDKs, automatic instrumentation technologies such as Beyla and SDK injection, or client-side OpenTelemetry Collectors. Each path presents different decisions, deployment requirements, configuration steps, and potential failure modes. You’ll define a coherent experience that helps users choose the right approach, complete setup successfully, troubleshoot problems, and understand whether their telemetry is healthy and useful. You’ll design a future in which a growing share of instrumentation work is performed by coding agents acting on behalf of developers. This means treating agents are first-class participants in the experience and ensuring that instrumentation options, configuration requirements, errors, and validation signals are structured, discoverable, and actionable by both humans and machines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your scope will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenTelemetry SDK onboarding and configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatic instrumentation experiences, including OBI/Beyla and SDK injection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-side OpenTelemetry Collector deployment and onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collector configuration, authentication, and initial connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guidance and machine-readable context that help people and agents choose the right instrumentation approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflows that allow coding-agents to implement, configure and verify instrumentation safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting missing, incomplete, malformed, or unhealthy telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validation signals that allow both people and agents to confirm that telemetry is healthy, correctly attributed, and usable in Grafana Cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The transition from receiving telemetry to activating the appropriate Grafana Cloud observability solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success does not stop when Grafana Cloud receives the first data point. Telemetry must arrive with the quality, context, and structure required to support meaningful observability outcomes. You’ll partner closely with teams responsible for experiences such as Application Observability, Kubernetes Monitoring, Infrastructure Observability, and Drilldown Apps to ensure OpenTelemetry workloads receive a first-class experience from initial setup through first value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a horizontal Staff-level product leadership role spanning multiple products and engineering teams. You may not directly own every SDK, collector, instrumentation technology, or downstream application involved in the journey. You will, however, be accountable for the coherence of the overall customer experience, its success measures, and the cross-product strategy required to improve it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI will also be part of how you work, not only what you build. You’ll be expected to use AI tools regularly to accelerate customer-research synthesis, analyze product signals, explore technical workflows, prototype experiences, develop positioning content, and test agent-led instrumentation journeys. You’ll model thoughtful, hands-on adoption of AI while applying strong judgement to its outputs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is not focused on developing OpenTelemetry as an open source project in isolation. You’ll engage with and contribute to the OpenTelemetry ecosystem where appropriate, while measuring success through customer activation and outcomes in Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the vision, strategy, and cross-product roadmap for the journey from an uninstrumented workload to healthy, useful telemetry in Grafana Cloud solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create coherent, opinionated experiences that help users choose and implement the right approach across SDK instrumentation, automatic instrumentation, and Collector-based deployment while preserving the flexibility advanced users require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and eliminate the leading causes of setup failure, abandonment, misconfiguration, and low-quality telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish shared experience principles, priorities, and success criteria across the product and engineering teams contributing to the OpenTelemetry journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer research, product data, and market insight to prioritize investments and measure outcomes such as onboarding completion, time to useful telemetry, telemetry health, and workload expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with downstream Grafana Cloud solution teams to create a coherent transition from telemetry ingestion to meaningful product activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend beyond product delivery to how the OpenTelemetry experience is positioned and brought to market. In partnership with Product Marketing and go-to-market teams, you’ll help define the product narrative, sharpen out differentiation, and develop launches, technical content, adoption programs, and campaigns that create demand and accelerate customer activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering, Design, Documentation, Developer Relations, Product Marketing, and go-to-market teams to deliver and communicate a differentiated OpenTelemetry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Grafana Labs and its customers in relevant OpenTelemetry ecosystem discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;What makes you a great fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Product Management experience, with a strong track record in developer tools, observability, infrastructure, data platforms, or another technically complex B2B product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading strategy and execution across multiple engineering teams or product areas without relying on direct organizational authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of OpenTelemetry, including SDK instrumentation, OTLP, Collector pipelines, telemetry context, and semantic conventions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or building instrumentation systems, agents, telemetry collectors, configuration products, or related infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the challenges involved in deploying and operating software across Kubernetes, virtual machines, and public cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning complex onboarding, configuration, and troubleshooting workflows into clear and approachable product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of using customer research and product data to make decisions, align stakeholders, and deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence technical and nontechnical stakeholders in a remote, globally distributed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to or building products around the OpenTelemetry or broader open source observability ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automatic instrumentation, eBPF, or runtime-based instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firsthand experience as an SRE, platform engineer, developer, or observability practitioner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building product-led onboarding, configuration-validation, or telemetry-health experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;In Germany, the base compensation range for this role is EUR 124,571 &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;- EUR 149,485&lt;/span&gt;. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
